// # xlang — FFI / Cross-Language Glue
//
// Logline: The dlopen-based FFI, the FFI security wrapper (cap-gated, minisign-verified), and the cross-language dispatch surface for emitting code that links against non-C targets.
//
// Setup: ffi.c is the generic dlopen/dlsym/dlclose; ffi_sec.c is the security wrapper (cap + minisign signature verification on the loaded .so); xlang.c is the higher-level cross-language dispatch.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Read ffi.c — dlopen/dlsym/dlclose.
//   2. Read ffi_sec.c — cap-gated, signature-verified FFI.
//   3. Read xlang.c — cross-language dispatch.
//
// ──▓▓ xlang ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: FFI is the highest-risk attack surface — every load is cap + signature gated ::
